// RESCUED 2026-09-15 from the stranded feat/converter-editor worktree (July 2026).
// Kept as a REFERENCE SCAFFOLD, not as a curated rule book. Its TabcToggleBtn ->
// tcxButton section was machine-generated: 241 links, several of them plainly wrong
// (e.g. HintHelper.HintWindow.PopupMenu <- PopupMenu maps a button's popup onto the
// hint window's). The curated book for that conversion is convrules\TabcToggleBtn-
// to-TcxButton.rules. Read this one for the DIRECTIVE FORMS it exercises, not for
// its mappings.
#convert Vcl.Graphics.TFont -> Vcl.Graphics.TFont
#note sample rule-book for ConvRulesEditor -- edit in the visual editor
#link Color <- Color
#link Height <- Height
#link Name <- Name
#link Size <- Size : Round
#default Charset = 1
#ignore Handle
#note Handle is an OS resource -- intentionally not mapped
// a hand comment survives round-trip
; so does a semicolon comment

#convert Vcl.StdCtrls.TEdit -> Vcl.StdCtrls.TMemo
#note second rule -- alternative target for the same family of controls
#link Text <- Text
